From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WLTB Gino <gino@wltb.local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:08:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] motor: free IRQs before draining debounce timers in teardown

The min/max position hardirqs are what arm the debounce timers
(mod_timer in motor.c :342/:383, firing the callbacks from softirq ~5ms
later; the callbacks dereference motor->pdata and gpio_get_value() the
min/max pins). Both the remove() path and the probe error path tore
down in orders that leave windows:

- remove() drained the timers before freeing the IRQs, so a late IRQ
  could re-arm a timer between del_timer_sync() and gpio_free(). Per
  motor the order is now free_irq() -> del_timer_sync() -> gpio_free().
- the probe error path freed the min/max GPIOs before free_irq() and
  drained the timers only after pdata was cleared. Same reorder
  applied there; a failed probe is rare, but the window was identical.

The timers are armed solely from those two handlers (grep mod_timer:
:342, :383 - no other arming sites), so after free_irq() the drain in
del_timer_sync() is final.

ingenic_tcu_counter_stop() still moves after misc_deregister():
stopping the counter first let a racing ioctl re-begin it. Note the
residual window is NOT closed: misc_deregister() does not revoke fds
already open, so a holder can still run fops across teardown. That is
the generic chardev teardown race present throughout this SDK; closing
it needs the probe/remove rework the vendor driver never had.

mutex_destroy() keeps its original first position and is no longer
dropped: dev_mutex is taken by real fops on this driver (:455, :482,
:497, :561), not just under CONFIG_DEBUG_MUTEXES.

The 3.10.14 ms419xx sibling has no position IRQs and no debounce
timers, so the reorder does not apply there.

Companion to 0005 (devres double-free). Regenerated against the
restructured thingino/ingenic-sdk layout at 5ed08a39, applied on top
of 0005.
Signed-off-by: WLTB Gino <gino@wltb.local>
---
diff --git a/4.4.94/misc/motor/motor.c b/4.4.94/misc/motor/motor.c
index 3b5d9715..8799ac34 100644
--- a/4.4.94/misc/motor/motor.c
+++ b/4.4.94/misc/motor/motor.c
@@ -982,12 +982,14 @@ error_min_gpio:
 		if(motor->pdata == NULL)
 			continue;
 		if (motor->min_pos_irq) {
-			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_min_gpio);
 			free_irq(motor->min_pos_irq, motor);
+			del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
+			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_min_gpio);
 		}
 		if (motor->max_pos_irq) {
-			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_max_gpio);
 			free_irq(motor->max_pos_irq, motor);
+			del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
+			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_max_gpio);
 		}
 		if (motor->pdata->motor_st1_gpio != -1)
 			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_st1_gpio);
@@ -1015,7 +1017,6 @@ static int motor_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	int i;
 	struct motor_device *mdev = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct motor_driver *motor = NULL;
-	ingenic_tcu_counter_stop(mdev->tcu);
 	mutex_destroy(&mdev->dev_mutex);
 
 	free_irq(mdev->run_step_irq, mdev);
@@ -1023,13 +1024,20 @@ static int motor_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		motor = &(mdev->motors[i]);
 		if(motor->pdata == NULL)
 			continue;
+		/* Free the min/max IRQs before draining the debounce
+		 * timers: the hardirq handlers mod_timer() these same
+		 * timers, so draining first would let a late IRQ re-arm
+		 * a timer that then runs after the pins are freed. The
+		 * timers are armed solely from those two handlers. */
 		if (motor->min_pos_irq) {
-			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_min_gpio);
 			free_irq(motor->min_pos_irq, motor);
+			del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
+			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_min_gpio);
 		}
 		if (motor->max_pos_irq) {
-			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_max_gpio);
 			free_irq(motor->max_pos_irq, motor);
+			del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
+			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_max_gpio);
 		}
 		if (motor->pdata->motor_st1_gpio != -1)
 			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_st1_gpio);
@@ -1047,8 +1055,6 @@ static int motor_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		motor->max_pos_irq = 0;
 		motor->min_pos_irq_cnt = 0;
 		motor->max_pos_irq_cnt = 0;
-		del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
-		del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
 	}
 
 	if (mdev->proc)
@@ -1056,6 +1062,7 @@ static int motor_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	misc_deregister(&mdev->misc_dev);
 
+	ingenic_tcu_counter_stop(mdev->tcu);
 	return 0;
 }
 
